Package: pcmt
Title: Permutation-Calibrated Conditional Independence Tests
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Ziang", "Niu", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "ziangniu@wharton.upenn.edu")
Description: Random-forest implementations of permutation-calibrated generalised
    covariance measure (GCM) and projected covariance measure (PCM) tests,
    together with adaptive resampling for multiple testing. Implements methods
    of Ai and Niu (2026) <doi:10.48550/arXiv.2611.03255>, building on the GCM of
    Shah and Peters (2020) <doi:10.1214/19-AOS1857> and the PCM of Lundborg et al.
    (2024) <doi:10.1214/24-AOS2447>. Uses the 'comets' regression infrastructure.
    Finite-sample validity holds when the exposure is independent of the outcome
    and covariates. Validity under conditional independence is asymptotic and
    requires nuisance-estimation and permutation-stability conditions.
License: GPL (>= 3)
URL: https://github.com/ZiangNiu6/pcmt,
    https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.03255
